{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-21837-r4512977","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Peruvian Molded Rice (Arroz Tapado)","sourcePageId":21837,"sourceRevision":"4512977","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T00:31:39Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Peruvian%20Molded%20Rice%20(Arroz%20Tapado)&oldid=4512977","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:18.668Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Gluten-free recipes","Category:Peruvian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using ground beef","Category:Recipes using hard-cooked egg","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using raisin","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes with metric units"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"4222412df9d4df84de046605ae67202cef8b94f8745ce77f616512be6066e7b9","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| category = Rice recipes\n| servings = 6\n| Difficulty = 2\n| time = 45 minutes|1\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Peru|Cuisine of Peru]]\n\n'''''Arroz tapado''''' (Spanish for molded rice) is very popular in Peru and is a favorite among children because the recipe calls for molding rice and minced beef into a shape.\n\nThe minced beef preparation is very similar to ''[[cookbook:picadillo|picadillo]]'' (Spanish for minced meat) which is popular throughout Latin America and the Philippines. In most other countries ''picadillo'' is served with white rice on the side.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 3 cloves of [[cookbook:garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[cookbook:olive oil|olive oil]]\n* [[cookbook:Lemon Juice|Lemon juice]]\n* [[cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (1 [[Cookbook:Liter|litre]]) water\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]] (450 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) washed [[cookbook:rice|rice]]\n* 1 [[cookbook:onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Pound|pounds]] (900 g) [[Cookbook:Ground Beef|ground beef]]\n* 2 [[cookbook:tomato|tomatoes]], finely chopped\n* 1 tbsp [[cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]]\n* 4 tbsp of [[cookbook:raisin|raisins]]\n* 5 [[Cookbook:Olive|black olives]], chopped\n* 3 [[cookbook:Hard Boiled Eggs|hard boiled eggs]]; 2 chopped, 1 whole\n* 1 tbsp [[cookbook:parsley|parsley]], finely minced\n==Preparation==\n# [[cookbook:Sauté|Sauté]] the garlic in oil, add a few drops of lemon juice, salt and the water, and bring to a [[cookbook:boil|boil]]. \n#Add rice and cook until tender. This should take 20–25 minutes.\n# In another pan, stir in onions and sauté. \n# Add meat, tomatoes, tomato paste, raisins, olives, egg and parsley.\n# Take an 8-ounce measuring cup and coat the inside with a little oil. Fill halfway with rice, add some meat filling and add more rice to top of cup. Invert onto a plate and carefully remove cup.\n#Cut the remaining hard-boiled egg in half and serve the two halves along side the ''arroz tapado'' on the same plate.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Use only the egg whites from the hard boiled egg and mince a low-fat cut of beef to reduce the fat at cholesterol in this dish.\n[[Category:Peruvian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground beef|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using raisin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Gluten-free recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using hard-cooked egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Peruvian Molded Rice (Arroz Tapado)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"6","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3 cloves of garlic, minced","sourceText":"3 cloves of garlic, minced","amountText":"3 cloves of garlic, minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tbsp olive oil","sourceText":"2 tbsp olive oil","amountText":"2 tbsp olive oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Lemon juice","sourceText":"Lemon juice","amountText":"Lemon juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Salt","sourceText":"Salt","amountText":"Salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"4 cups (1 litre) water","sourceText":"4 cups (1 litre) water","amountText":"4 cups (1 litre) water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 pound (450 g) washed rice","sourceText":"1 pound (450 g) washed rice","amountText":"1 pound (450 g) washed rice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 onion, finely chopped","sourceText":"1 onion, finely chopped","amountText":"1 onion, finely chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 pounds (900 g) ground beef","sourceText":"2 pounds (900 g) ground beef","amountText":"2 pounds (900 g) ground beef","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"2 tomatoes, finely chopped","sourceText":"2 tomatoes, finely chopped","amountText":"2 tomatoes, finely chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"1 tbsp tomato paste","sou